From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alpha-liu-01 <116528196+alpha-liu-01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:32:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] msm: camera: sensor: continue power-up when a shared
 GPIO is busy

All sensors and the flash use TLMM pin 38 as their VIO enable, which the
device tree does not mark as shared. Powering up a second camera device
got -EBUSY on that GPIO, the power-up was aborted, and CamX failed in
CSLAcquireDevice.

When the GPIO table request fails with -EBUSY, log it and continue, as
Xiaomi's prebuilt camera.ko does; any other GPIO error still aborts. The
pin is already driven by its holder, and custom_gpio1_powernum keeps it
up until the last user powers down.
---
 .../cam_sensor_utils/cam_sensor_util.c        | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/techpack/camera/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_sensor_utils/cam_sensor_util.c b/techpack/camera/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_sensor_utils/cam_sensor_util.c
index c3aa37eed..29c8f3416 100644
--- a/techpack/camera/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_sensor_utils/cam_sensor_util.c
+++ b/techpack/camera/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_sensor_utils/cam_sensor_util.c
@@ -2066,6 +2066,10 @@ int cam_sensor_core_power_up(struct cam_sensor_power_ctrl_t *ctrl,
 	rc = cam_sensor_util_request_gpio_table(soc_info, 1);
 	if (rc < 0) {
 		no_gpio = rc;
+		if (rc == -EBUSY)
+			CAM_INFO(CAM_SENSOR,
+				"%s: a gpio is held by another camera device (shared), still do power up",
+				soc_info->dev_name);
 	}
 
 	if (ctrl->cam_pinctrl_status) {
@@ -2155,7 +2159,20 @@ int cam_sensor_core_power_up(struct cam_sensor_power_ctrl_t *ctrl,
 		case SENSOR_STANDBY:
 		case SENSOR_CUSTOM_GPIO1:
 		case SENSOR_CUSTOM_GPIO2:
-			if (no_gpio) {
+			/*
+			 * stone-ut: -EBUSY means another camera device holds
+			 * one of this table's pins. On sunstone every sensor
+			 * and the flash share TLMM 38 (CAM_VIO*, CUSTOM_GPIO1),
+			 * the DT's gpios-shared does not list it, and CamX
+			 * powers the wide and depth sensors together for
+			 * camera 0 (logical bokeh camera). The pin is already
+			 * driven by its holder, and custom_gpio1_powernum keeps
+			 * it up until the last user powers down. Xiaomi's
+			 * camera.ko continues the same way ("request gpio
+			 * failed,still do power up"); aborting here makes CamX
+			 * abort in CSLAcquireDevice and the provider restart.
+			 */
+			if (no_gpio && no_gpio != -EBUSY) {
 				if (power_setting->seq_type != SENSOR_CUSTOM_GPIO1) {
 					CAM_ERR(CAM_SENSOR, "request gpio failed");
 					goto power_up_failed;
